The receipt on stdout is a unified diff of the whole file: the plan path on both the `--- `
and `+++ ` headers, an `@@` hunk header offset to the change, and three lines of context
either side — so an untouched body never reaches the diff.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
type: feature
status: backlog
sp: 5
owner: nobody
retro: null
---
# My Plan

Body text.
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md sp=8
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 title: Foo
 type: feature
 status: backlog
-sp: 5
+sp: 8
 owner: nobody
 retro: null
 ---
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: sp=8
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
type: feature
status: backlog
sp: 8
owner: nobody
retro: null
---
# My Plan

Body text.
